diff --git a/docs/ops/logging.md b/docs/ops/logging.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..85177a2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Logging and ops alerts
+
+Observability is split into three lanes. Each has one job, one destination, and
+one decision rule. When in doubt, use the decision guide below.
+
+| Lane | Destination | Use it for | Code |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ---- |
+| **Archive** | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily rotation, 14 days) | Routine application logs, debug to error | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) |
+| **Audit** | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily rotation, 90 days, min level `info`) | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` |
+| **Alert** | Discord incoming webhook | A human must be paged about an actionable production incident | `app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(...)` |
+
+Discord is **not** a log channel. There is no `discord` entry in
+`config/logging.php`, and nothing sends to Discord unless code explicitly calls
+`DiscordOpsAlert::send()`. Logging an error does not page anyone.
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. **Would someone have to act on it right now?** (a job exhausted its retries,
+   a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity)
+   → **Alert** (`DiscordOpsAlert`). Also write it to the archive, since an alert
+   is not searchable history.
+2. **Is it a record of a human or system decision about business state?** (role
+   change, subscription transition, login lockout, refund requested)
+   → **Audit** (`Log::channel('audit')`). Log the who, what, and when in the
+   context. Audit is not for debugging noise.
+3. **Anything else** (request traces, debug info, handled exceptions, timings)
+   → **Archive** (`Log::`).
+
+An event can belong to more than one lane. For example, a subscription that
+fails to renew can be an audit entry (the state transition) and an alert (the
+on-call needs to know). Each lane is called explicitly; the lanes never forward
+to each other.
+
+## Archive: `daily`
+
+- `LOG_STACK` (default `daily`) selects the channels behind the `stack` default
+  channel. The `stack` channel now writes to `daily`, not `single`.
+- `LOG_LEVEL` sets the minimum level (default `debug`).
+- `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` sets retention in days (default `14`).
+
+## Audit: `audit`
+
+- Written with `Log::channel('audit')`. It is separate from the archive: entries
+  do **not** also appear in `laravel.log`.
+- `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` sets the minimum level (default `info`, so `debug` is dropped).
+- `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` sets retention in days (default `90`).
+- Put identifiers and state in the context, never a message string built from
+  user input:
+
+```php
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'subscription_id' => $subscription->id,
+    'from' => $previous,
+    'to' => $subscription->status,
+    'actor_id' => $request->user()->id,
+]);
+```
+
+Never put secrets, card data, or raw PII in any lane (see below).
+
+## Alert: `DiscordOpsAlert`
+
+`App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` (`app/Ops/DiscordOpsAlert.php`) is a plain class
+resolved from the container with no constructor arguments.
+
+```php
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Asaas webhook failing',           // title
+    'Webhook processing exhausted retries',  // message
+    ['entity_id' => 42, 'queue' => 'asaas-webhooks'],  // optional context
+);
+```
+
+The Discord text is the title, the message, then one `key=value` line per
+context entry, truncated to 1800 characters.
+
+- **Configuration:** `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` (read as `services.discord.webhook_url`).
+  When it is empty or unset, `send()` is a silent no-op: no HTTP request is made.
+  Local and test environments leave it empty.
+- **Transport:** `POST` JSON `{"content": "..."}` to the configured URL, with a
+  5-second timeout. No embeds, mentions, retries, or rate limiting.
+- **Soft-fail:** `send()` never throws. A non-2xx answer or a transport error is
+  written to the archive as an `error` entry, `Discord ops alert failed`. The
+  entry includes the HTTP status or the exception class and a message with the
+  webhook URL scrubbed out. The webhook URL embeds a token, so it must never
+  appear in a log.
+- **Redaction** (the payload must not leak secrets):
+  - a context value whose key contains `password`, `token`, `secret`,
+    `authorization`, `api_key` / `api-key` / `apikey`, or `webhook`
+    (case-insensitive) becomes `[redacted]`;
+  - any string value containing `Bearer <credential>` becomes `[redacted]`,
+    whatever its key, including in the title and message;
+  - nested arrays are redacted recursively and rendered as JSON.
+
+Alerts are for incidents only. Do not send routine events, and do not send a
+second alert for the same ongoing incident.
+
+## Rules for agents and developers
+
+- Logging an error is not paging. Page with `DiscordOpsAlert` only for an
+  actionable incident.
+- Audit entries are durable records. Put state in the context; never log secrets,
+  tokens, card data, or raw PII.
+- Do not add a `discord` Monolog channel or forward `Log::` entries to Discord.
+- Audit events go to `Log::channel('audit')`, not to the archive. Do not record
+  them in `laravel.log` in place of the audit lane.
+
+## Environment keys
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | ------- | ------- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the `stack` default channel |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Minimum level for the archive (`daily`) |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level for the audit lane |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | _(empty)_ | Discord incoming webhook for `DiscordOpsAlert`; empty disables alerts |
+
+The test environment pins `LOG_STACK=daily` in `phpunit.xml`, so the suite does
+not depend on a local `.env`.
